.TH SHULID 8 "August 2026" "shuli" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
shulid \- WiFi authentication daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shulid
.RI [ config ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shulid
is a pure-Rust WiFi authentication daemon implementing
WPA3-Personal (SAE), OWE (RFC 8110), and open
authentication.  It performs the full authentication flow
in userspace: scan, authentication, association, 4-way
handshake, and key installation via nl80211.  Data-frame
encryption (CCMP) is handled by the kernel once keys are
installed.
.PP
On successful authentication the link is brought up and
.B shulid
holds the connection, handling group rekey (in userspace or
offloaded to the driver when supported).  An external DHCP
client can be used to obtain an address.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I config
Path to the YAML configuration file.
Default:
.IR /etc/shuli/config.yml .
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is YAML:
.PP
.RS
.nf
interfaces:
  - name: wlan0
    type: wifi-phy
    wifi:
      ssid: MyNetwork
      password: "secretpass"
.fi
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Cleanly disconnect from the AP and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Connection was established and held until a shutdown signal.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (configuration, netlink, or shutdown before
connection was established).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hostapd (8),
.BR wpa_supplicant (8),
.BR iwd (8)
